buffer_cache: download only the Preflushable pages of a GPU write at fences

From Lichii PR 104 (fc12c793e, merge 0bf0f834b) by Zarigis. One hunk rewritten: our
MarkWrittenBuffer adds the range through Nx2AddRangeOnce.

A GPU write that covered any Preflushable page was queued whole. A native storage
binding is sized from its mapping (up to 8 MiB since 2e12e0def), so one page the guest
CPU had read sent the whole binding to a staging buffer at every fence. Run38 ran out
of memory in that path: CreateStagingBuffer from CommitAsyncFlushesHigh. Upstream PR 609
measured the same readback on Mario Kart World at 7.2-7.8 GiB/s. Now just the marked
pages are queued and read traps are armed on the rest. The binding keeps its size, so
no access is dropped, unlike PR 609.

EDEN_NX2_EXACT_PREFLUSH=0 restores the old behaviour.

